# Ask before pushing

After a requested code change is finished and checked, commit it on the current branch. Do not push to GitHub until the user says yes.

- Ask in one short sentence before any `git push`.
- Skip the commit when the task was only a question, or when there is nothing to commit.
- Follow the repository commit style: one or two sentences about why the change exists.
- Do not force-push, skip hooks, or change git config.
- Do not commit secrets such as `.env` or credential files.
